  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f424be585f9e04c79a96c8292e8b9db1, type: 3}
  m_Name: Evento_EspeculacaoImobiliaria
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Metis.Runtime::KnowledgeEntryData
  _title: "Especula\xE7\xE3o Imobili\xE1ria"
  _titleEn: Real Estate Speculation
  _category: 1
  _unlockTrigger: 0
  _summary: "Quando um bairro se valoriza, os alugu\xE9is sobem e os moradores mais
    pobres acabam saindo, um processo chamado gentrifica\xE7\xE3o."
  _summaryEn: When a neighborhood gains value, rents rise and poorer residents end
    up leaving, a process called gentrification.
  _realWorld: "O Estatuto da Cidade, de 2001, prev\xEA instrumentos contra a especula\xE7\xE3o,
    como o IPTU progressivo para im\xF3veis vazios e as zonas especiais de interesse
    social, que reservam \xE1reas para moradia popular."
  _realWorldEn: Brazil's 2001 City Statute provides tools against speculation, such
    as a progressive property tax on vacant properties and special social interest
    zones that reserve land for affordable housing.
  _tradeOffs: "Valoriza\xE7\xE3o traz arrecada\xE7\xE3o, mas sem moradia acess\xEDvel
    a cidade expulsa quem a sustenta."
  _tradeOffsEn: Rising values bring revenue, but without affordable housing the city
    pushes out the people who keep it running.
  _sources:
  - Label: "Gentrifica\xE7\xE3o (Wikip\xE9dia)"
    Url: https://pt.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gentrifica%C3%A7%C3%A3o
  - Label: Estatuto da Cidade, Lei 10.257/2001 (Planalto)
    Url: https://www.planalto.gov.br/ccivil_03/leis/leis_2001/l10257.htm
